From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duelists Kingdom Engine <engine@duelistskingdom.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reset the opponent of an operation-based disabled zone effect
 when its card leaves

An operation-based EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD effect (Ojama King) keeps the opponent of
its zone prompt in disfield_opp. card::reset cleared the value on leave but kept
that opponent, so at n > 2 outside FFA4 the next stay on the field blocked the
zones of the first opponent while the prompt offered another one. The reset now
clears disfield_opp, disfield_selected and disfield_operation_opp of an effect with
an operation, so the next operation picks again. n_duelists > 2 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019EpX1AcvnigK9dTsxAa5W9
---
diff --git a/card.cpp b/card.cpp
index 81836ff..3649bf9 100644
--- a/card.cpp
+++ b/card.cpp
@@ -2057,8 +2057,18 @@ void card::reset(uint32_t id, uint32_t reset_type) {
 			battled_cards.clear();
 			reset_effect_count();
 			auto pr = field_effect.equal_range(EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD);
-			for(; pr.first != pr.second; ++pr.first)
-				pr.first->second->value = 0;
+			for(; pr.first != pr.second; ++pr.first) {
+				auto* peff = pr.first->second;
+				peff->value = 0;
+				// n > 2: the opponent that the zone prompt of the operation recorded belongs to the zones that this
+				// reset cleared, so the operation of the next stay on the field picks again. Effects without an
+				// operation keep the opponent that they registered.
+				if(pduel->game_field->n_duelists > 2 && peff->operation) {
+					peff->disfield_opp = DUELIST_NONE;
+					peff->disfield_selected = false;
+					peff->disfield_operation_opp = DUELIST_NONE;
+				}
+			}
 		}
 		if(id & (RESET_TODECK | RESET_TOHAND | RESET_TOGRAVE | RESET_REMOVE | RESET_TEMP_REMOVE
 			| RESET_OVERLAY | RESET_MSCHANGE | RESET_TOFIELD  | RESET_TURN_SET)) {
